IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art8-retention.l4: tests of Article 8(6), "retain for 10 years ... a copy of" four kinds of document (src:249-253), and of the Minister's powers to prescribe by Order.
-- The Article gives no starting point for the ten years (F3.1), does not say whether the day of the event is counted (F3.4) and says nothing of 29 February (F3.5).
-- The expected days are computed by hand from the convention each reading names, never from the output:
--   favoured: the day of the event is not counted, so the tenth anniversary is the last day of the period and the copy may be discarded on the day after it;
--   F3.4 reading B: the day of the event is the first day, so the day before the tenth anniversary is the last day, and the copy may be discarded on the anniversary.

§ `Tests of Article 8(6): retention for ten years`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

GIVEN k IS A `Document of a kind within Article 8(6)`
      received IS A DATE
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
`a copy of kind` k `received on` received `and ceasing to be operative on` ceased MEANS
    `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` WITH
        kind IS k
        `date received or made` IS received
        `date it ceased to be operative` IS ceased

`the constitution received on 1 March 2019` MEANS `a copy of kind` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` `received on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING
`the constitution received on 1 March 2019 and amended on 15 June 2021` MEANS `a copy of kind` `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it` `received on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and ceasing to be operative on` (JUST (YMD 2021 6 15))
`a return received on 31 December 2019` MEANS `a copy of kind` `an annual return of the charity` `received on` (YMD 2019 12 31) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING
`a notice served on the charity on 10 January 2024` MEANS `a copy of kind` `a notice served on the charity under this Law` `received on` (YMD 2024 1 10) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING
`a document prescribed by Order received on 1 March 2019` MEANS `a copy of kind` `a document prescribed by the Minister by Order` `received on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING
`a notice served on a governor on 10 January 2024` MEANS `a copy of kind` `a document of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list` `received on` (YMD 2024 1 10) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING
`a copy received on 29 February 2016` MEANS `a copy of kind` `an annual return of the charity` `received on` (YMD 2016 2 29) `and ceasing to be operative on` NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`discardable from` d MEANS `the copy may be discarded on and after` d

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` interp copy MEANS `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` interp copy `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019`

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      copy IS A `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))`
GIVETH AN `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))`
`for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` interp copy MEANS `Art 8(6) the Commissioner may discard the copy on` interp copy `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024`

§§ `F3.1 reading A (favoured): ten years from the day each copy is received or made`

-- Received 1 March 2019: the tenth anniversary is 1 March 2029, the last day of the ten years; it may be discarded from 2 March 2029.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 3 2)
-- Received 31 December 2019: the anniversary is 31 December 2029; from 1 January 2030.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `a return received on 31 December 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2030 1 1)
-- Each kind that Article 8(6) lists runs the same ten years: (a) the constitution and its amendments, (b) a return, (c) a notice served on the charity, (d) a prescribed document.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `a notice served on the charity on 10 January 2024` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2034 1 11)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `a document prescribed by Order received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 3 2)
-- A copy of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list: the notice served on a GOVERNOR is noted under 8(3)(k) but is not named in 8(6)(c) ("served on the charity").
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `a notice served on a governor on 10 January 2024` EQUALS `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained`
-- Whether the charity is still registered makes no difference to this reading.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 3 2)

§§ `F3.4: is the day of the event counted?`

-- Reading B: the day of the event is the first day of the ten years, so the period ends on the day before the anniversary and the copy may be discarded on the anniversary.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.4 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 3 1)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.4 reading B` `a return received on 31 December 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 12 31)
-- The two readings differ by one day, always.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` ((YMD 2029 3 1) PLUS 1)

§§ `F3.5: a copy received on 29 February`

-- Received 29 February 2016.  Favoured: the tenth anniversary is moved back to 28 February 2026, so from 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `a copy received on 29 February 2016` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- F3.5 reading B: the anniversary rolls forward to 1 March 2026, so from 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.5 reading B` `a copy received on 29 February 2016` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2026 3 2)
-- With the day of the event counted: the anniversary itself, 28 February 2026 (moved back) or 1 March 2026 (rolled).
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.4 reading B` `a copy received on 29 February 2016` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.4 reading B with F3.5 reading B` `a copy received on 29 February 2016` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- F3.5 changes nothing for a date that exists in the target year.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.5 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2029 3 2)

§§ `F3.1 reading B: ten years from the deregistration of the charity`

-- A charity that is still registered: none of its copies may be discarded yet.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `a return received on 31 December 2019` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
-- Deregistered on 1 June 2024: ten years from then, whatever the date of the copy.  The tenth anniversary is 1 June 2034; from 2 June 2034.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2034 6 2)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `a notice served on the charity on 10 January 2024` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2034 6 2)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `a notice served on a governor on 10 January 2024` EQUALS `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained`

§§ `F3.1 reading C: ten years from the day the copy ceases to be operative`

-- A constitution never amended and a charity still registered: it is still the operative constitution.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
-- The same constitution amended on 15 June 2021: ten years from the amendment; the anniversary is 15 June 2031, so from 16 June 2031.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019 and amended on 15 June 2021` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2031 6 16)
-- Never amended, but the charity is deregistered on 1 June 2024: it ceases to be operative with the deregistration; from 2 June 2034.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2034 6 2)
-- Amended and then deregistered: the amendment is the earlier end, so the 2021 date governs the superseded text.
#ASSERT `for Alpha, deregistered on 1 June 2024, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019 and amended on 15 June 2021` EQUALS `discardable from` (YMD 2031 6 16)

-- The three readings of F3.1 on one copy: the constitution received on 1 March 2019, never amended, the charity still registered, asked in 2029.
-- A: from 2 March 2029.  B and C: not while the charity remains registered.
#ASSERT NOT (`for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019`)
#ASSERT NOT (`for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019`)
#ASSERT `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` EQUALS `for Alpha, still registered, the earliest day for` `interpretation F3.1 reading C` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019`

§§ `The duty: the Commissioner must not discard a copy within the ten years`

-- Favoured reading, the constitution received on 1 March 2019: the prohibition holds through 1 March 2029 (the last day of the period) and is spent on 2 March 2029.
-- Discarded on the last day of the period: a breach.
-- EXPECT: BREACH | the copy was discarded within the retention period
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 3 1))

-- Discarded on the first day on which it may be: no breach.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 3 2))

-- Discarded soon after receipt: a breach.
-- EXPECT: BREACH | the copy was discarded within the retention period
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 2))

-- Never discarded and the ten years run out: spent, nothing owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 3 2)))

-- On the last day the prohibition still stands, with no day left.
-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST NOT `discard a copy of a document`
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 3 1)))

-- The other reading of the day of the event (F3.4 B): the prohibition ends a day sooner.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `interpretation F3.4 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 3 1))

-- EXPECT: BREACH | the copy was discarded within the retention period
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `interpretation F3.4 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2029 2 28))

-- A copy that Article 8(6) does not list: no duty, so discarding it is no breach.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` fav `a notice served on a governor on 10 January 2024` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2024 1 10)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2024 1 11))

-- F3.1 B, a charity still registered: no copy may be discarded, however long ago it was received.
-- EXPECT: BREACH | the copy was discarded within the retention period
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2060 1 1))

-- F3.1 B, deregistered on 1 June 2024: the ten years end on 1 June 2034.
-- EXPECT: BREACH | the copy was discarded within the retention period
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2034 6 1))

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6) the Commissioner must retain the copy for 10 years` `interpretation F3.1 reading B` `the constitution received on 1 March 2019` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2019 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `discard a copy of a document` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2034 6 2))

§§ `The Minister's powers to prescribe by Order (8(3)(n), 8(5)(e), 8(6)(d))`

-- A power is a permission: exercised, it is discharged; unexercised, it stands and is no breach.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(3)(n) the Minister may by Order prescribe other information to be entered in the register` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order prescribing` `other information to be entered in the register in respect of a registered charity` AT 10

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `make an Order prescribing`
#TRACE `Art 8(3)(n) the Minister may by Order prescribe other information to be entered in the register` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(5)(e) the Minister may by Order prescribe other matters to be entered in the historic section` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order prescribing` `other matters to be entered in the historic section` AT 10

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `make an Order prescribing`
#TRACE `Art 8(5)(e) the Minister may by Order prescribe other matters to be entered in the historic section` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(6)(d) the Minister may by Order prescribe other documents to be retained` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make an Order prescribing` `other documents of which a copy is to be retained` AT 10

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MAY `make an Order prescribing`
#TRACE `Art 8(6)(d) the Minister may by Order prescribe other documents to be retained` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
